soft green bokeh, creating a gentle and intimate feeling of quietly watching her from nearby. Late afternoon golden sunlight falls from the side and slightly behind her, soft and warm, tracing a bright rim along her hair while her face stays evenly lit; warm yellow and fresh green tones with gentle saturation fill the frame, the whole scene glowing with a sweet and nostalgic summer mood. An innocent and pure young girl of about eighteen, East Asian, fair soft skin with a natural matte finish, slim and petite with a light youthful frame, sweet and healing at first sight. Her black waist-length straight hair is half-tied with a white satin ribbon, neat air bangs brushing her eyebrows, a few fine strands swaying beside her cheeks in the breeze. Makeup is a barely-there pure style - a touch of under-eye blush and pale pink lip tint, as if she wears nothing at all. Her bright clear eyes are fixed on the pinwheel, lips pushed into a soft pout aimed at the little blades, cheeks rounded with effort, her whole face brimming with playful concentration and untouched sweetness. She wears a white cotton blouse with a small round Peter Pan collar and gentle puff sleeves ending in delicate elastic cuffs, the cotton absorbing the light in a clean matte finish; a pastel blue pinafore skirt with two small buttons on the front straps sits over the blouse, its hem flaring loosely around her thighs, white frilly ankle socks peeking above a pair of simple white canvas shoes with loosely tied laces, a thin silver bracelet resting on her raised wrist. She stands with one hand raised high gripping the stick of a colorful little pinwheel, its paper blades catching flecks of sunlight, her weight shifted onto one leg, head tilted slightly as she rounds her cheeks to blow. Around her spreads a sunlit park lawn, dappled light filtering through the blurred trees behind her, a wooden bench and a few fallen leaves dotting the grass in soft blur. The composition uses the rule of thirds, placing her 